Wow. I think that's actually a good catch for another soundness issue that I completely missed.

I tried very hard to think if the previous `BorrowAsAtomicModeGuard` was sound. But I missed a counterexample. Your code gives me more insight.

It's pretty easy:
```rust
struct AtomicModeGuard;

trait BorrowAsAtomicModeGuard {
    fn borrow(&self) -> &AtomicModeGuard;
}

struct FakeGuard;

impl BorrowAsAtomicModeGuard for FakeGuard {
    fn borrow(&self) -> &AtomicModeGuard {
        todo!()
    }
}
```

*We really need to run the `as_atomic_mode_guard` method first before assuming we're in atomic mode!*
